0..60 Comment "// A case on a parameter whose goal reads a later parameter."
61..63 Comment "//"
64..138 Comment "// The type of the later parameter reads the scrutinee, and the goal reads"
139..214 Comment "// both. The map over the arguments of a signature has this shape: its goal"
215..292 Comment "// reads the signature and the arguments, and the type of the arguments reads"
293..310 Comment "// the signature."
311..313 Comment "//"
314..389 Comment "// The checker generalises the case\'s motive over each later binder that an"
390..466 Comment "// arm or the motive reads and whose type reads the scrutinee. Each arm then"
467..543 Comment "// meets the later binder at its own constructor. Here no arm reads `v`, and"
544..573 Comment "// the motive alone reads it."
574..576 Comment "//"
577..592 Comment "// - see: #5324"
593..663 Comment "// - see: #3483 — the generalisation over a binder that an arm reads"
